}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Winter Commander Kaihime''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Winter Commander Kaihime stands out from most Seasonal Ubers, as she's extremely good, and much better than even her normal variant thanks to her [[Surge Attack]]. While mainly advertised as a crowd-controlling unit, her real strength lies in her disgustingly high damage output. At just Lv.30, she has ~7.4k DPS assuming her Surge always lands, and her [[Savage Blow]] further boosts that to an average of ~11k DPS, which is insanely high. At Lv.50, she has ~11.7k DPS with her Surge, which gets boosted to an average DPS of ~17.5k with Savage Blow. Even her somewhat inconsistent Surge Attack spawn radius can also be turned into an advantage, occasionally sniping backlines and devastating them if she happens to Savage Blow as well.

Winter Commander Kaihime's [[Slow]] ability is admittedly rather mediocre, but suffices for how much she makes up for it in other aspects. It has about a 50% uptime (effectively 25% when accounting for its activation rate), but does target two of the most common traits in the game, providing at least provide some bonus value if using her in a stage with Red or Floating enemies.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner & Sniper}}

